From: jempa <jempamartensson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:28:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] USD light behavior: distant light angular size, emitter
 camera visibility, image tint, emitting interface shapes, shaping frame (for
 hdPbrt)

- DistantLight "float hdpbrtangle" (angular diameter): radiance L inside a cone, sampled
  uniformly; such a light is an infinite light that escaping rays hit. Camera rays do not
  see the disc.
- Area lights on "interface" shapes are kept: they emit but do not block or shadow.
- DiffuseAreaLight "bool hdpbrtcamera" (hide the emitter from camera rays) and
  "rgb hdpbrttint" (multiplies an emission image).
- Light shaping "float shapingframe" [9]: rotation from the light frame to the shaping
  frame, for shapes written in a rotated frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
